\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Qualitative comparison at $\times 4$ on texture-dense hard samples. The top reference strip shows the ground-truth images with the crop regions; the rows below magnify those regions for Bicubic, IMDN, SwinIR-light, SRFormer-light, CATANet, DPRNet (ours), and the ground truth. DPRNet restores repetitive building grids and high-contrast line art with clear structure, visually comparable to the strongest content-routing baseline on these challenging crops. The samples are chosen by high-frequency content rather than by per-crop DPRNet advantage, and quantitative PSNR/SSIM are reported in Table~\ref {tab:main_comparison}.}}{13}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
